# Nothing here is ever line-ending converted.
#
# The suite proves that every committed .bf is byte for byte what tools/bfgen
# makes of its skeleton, and that every .bf contains only the eight brainfuck
# command bytes and whitespace. A CRLF checkout breaks the first check on every
# fixture at once while leaving the second green, because \r is whitespace and
# is not a command byte -- so the symptom points at the expander, which is
# fine, and says nothing about the clone that actually caused it.
#
# The protocol makes it worse than it is in the sibling: brainstem's frames are
# binary, and a fixture that emits 0x0a is emitting a length byte or a payload
# byte, not a line ending. Anything that rewrites 0x0a on the way to disk is
# corrupting data, not formatting text.
#
# So autocrlf is refused here rather than left to whatever the clone was
# configured with.
* -text
